        "original_id": "78b88dfe-ef6f-5255-b815-ec129774d570",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Concepts: Murabaha, markup, fiqh, cost-plus pricing\n- Topics: Islamic jurisprudence, sales contracts, pricing\n\nFacts:\n- Murabaha is a term in fiqh, or Islamic jurisprudence, for a sales contract in which the buyer and seller agree on the markup or cost-plus price for the items being sold.\n- Murabaha is derived from the Arabic word \"ribh,\" which means profit.\n- Markup is the ratio between the cost of a good or service and its selling price.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "bbb5250c-8713-51ae-8316-2ae89cf8a92b",
        "text": "Page: Murabaha. Sentence: Murabaḥah, murabaḥa or murâbaḥah (Arabic: مرابحة‎ ‎ , derived from \"ribh\" Arabic: ربح‎ ‎ , meaning profit) is a term of \"fiqh\" (Islamic jurisprudence) for a sales contract where the buyer and seller agree on the markup (profit) or \"cost-plus\" price for the item(s) being sold.\nPage: Markup (business). Sentence: Markup is the ratio between the cost of a good or service and its selling price.",
